## 1. What the tools do

Two tools run from one program. A person starts each tool by hand on a Nelnet laptop. Nothing runs by itself.

The weekly check reads saved Jira filters. The US instance has two. It groups the issues by project. It makes a Confluence page. It can send one email to the Odd Squad mailbox with the page link.

The structure report reads the Jira queries on the structure page in Confluence. It finds the assignee and the reporter of each issue that the queries return. It sends one email to those people with the page link. It sends a list of issues with no reachable person to a team mailbox.

The tools make no model call. They do not keep Jira data on disk. The structure report writes two local files for a dry run and a test send. Section 7 describes them.

## 2. What you need

- Python 3.13 on the laptop.
- A Jira personal access token and a Confluence personal access token for your own account.
- Permission to view the saved filters and the structure page.
- Permission to add comments on the tracking ticket.
- Permission to create pages under the parent page in Confluence.
- For the structure report: permission to send as the mailbox, and the SMTP password. [TBD: the send as permission is not granted yet]

